<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>DiagnosticCatalog.StyleCop</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>DiagnosticCatalog.StyleCop</RootNamespace>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    NO <ReleaseTrain> yet, deliberately, and this is the one thing to fix before this catalog
    can ship.

    It belongs on the 'stylecop' train, but joining it now would make the project packable while it
    still carries a ProjectReference to DiagnosticCatalog on the 'lib' train — the construct
    ADR-0007 forbids, because `dotnet pack` would stamp a dependency on a lib version that was
    never published and every consumer's restore would fail with NU1102 on an immutable artifact.

    The foundation has no published version to reference yet, so the release order ADR-0007
    implies has not run its first step. Once lib ships, this project swaps the ProjectReference
    below for a versionless PackageReference to DiagnosticCatalog and declares
    declares its release train as 'stylecop'. Until then it builds and is testable, but
    publishes nothing — which is honest rather than convenient.

    The train name is spelled in prose above, never as the XML element: tools/trains.sh
    discovers membership with a line-oriented sed that does not parse XML, so the element
    written inside this comment would be read as a real declaration and this project would
    be packed after all.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Label="Package">
    <PackageId>DiagnosticCatalog.StyleCop</PackageId>
    <DevelopmentDependency>false</DevelopmentDependency>
    <Title>DiagnosticCatalog.StyleCop</Title>
    <Description>The StyleCop.Analyzers rules as strongly referenced constants, so that SuppressMessageAttribute takes compile-checked references instead of magic strings. Ids, categories and help links are read from the analyzers' own DiagnosticDescriptor instances. Unofficial; not affiliated with the StyleCop.Analyzers project.</Description>
    <PackageTags>roslyn;analyzers;diagnostics;suppressmessage;stylecop;code-analysis;catalog</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <Authors>Reefact</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) Reefact</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Reefact/diagnostic-catalog</PackageProjectUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Update="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../DiagnosticCatalog/DiagnosticCatalog.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
